hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16759","He said: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from al-Shabi, from Abu Jubayra ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari, from uncles of his: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, and there was none of us but he had a nickname or two nicknames; he said: When he called him by his nickname we would say: O Messenger of Allah, he dislikes this; he said: So there was revealed: And do not insult one another by nicknames."
"23615","I found in my father's book in his handwriting: Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us from al-Sha'bi from Abu Jubayrah ibn al-Dahhak al-Ansari from paternal uncles of his: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came, and there was none of us except he had one or two nicknames; when he called a man by his nickname we said: O Messenger of Allah, he dislikes this; so there was revealed: And do not insult one another by nicknames."
"23616","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Sulayman, a righteous shaykh of good appearance, a Madinan, narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Abdullah ibn Khubayb narrated to us from his father from his uncle, he said: We were in a gathering, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us with a trace of water on his head, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, we see you cheerful. He said: Yes. Then the people discussed wealth, and the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: There is no harm in wealth for one who fears Allah, and health for one who fears Allah is better than wealth, and cheerfulness is from bliss."
"23617","Abu Amir narrated to us, Abbad ya'ni Ibn Rashid narrated to us from al-Hasan from a man from Banu Sulayt that he passed by the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was sitting at the door of his mosque reclining on his arms, wearing a cotton garment with no other garment upon him, saying: The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim, he does not wrong him nor forsake him; then he pointed with his hand to his chest, saying: Taqwa is here, taqwa is here."
"23618","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Za'idah narrated to us, al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi' ibn Umaylah narrated to us from Abu Amr al-Shaybani from a man from the Ansar from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Horses are three: a horse a man ties in the path of Allah Almighty, so its price is reward, its riding is reward, its lending is reward, and its fodder is reward; and a horse upon which a man gambles and bets, so its price is sin, its fodder is sin, and its riding is sin; and a horse for the belly, so perhaps it will be a barrier against poverty, Allah Almighty willing."
